-- title:
--   Finite vertex stabilisers and finitely many vertex orbits
-- statement:
--   Let $r$ be a prime and let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero domain which is a discrete valuation ring, complete for the $\pi$-adic topology at an irreducible element $\pi$, with residue ring $\mathcal O/(\pi)$ of cardinality $r$ and $(r)=(\pi)$; let $K_0$ be a characteristic-zero fraction field of $\mathcal O$. Let $Onr$ be a characteristic-zero $\mathcal O$-domain with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $Fr$, complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, that ideal being maximal, such that every element of $Onr$ satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi$, every monic polynomial over $Onr$ of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi$, and $Fr(x)\equiv x^{r}$ modulo $\pi$. Let $vdet:\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)\to\mathbb Z$ (multiplicative) satisfy $vdet(g)=n$ exactly when $\det g=u\pi^{n}$ for some $u\in\mathcal O^\times$. Let $\bar r\neq r$ be a prime, $N\neq 0$ with $r\nmid N$, and $a_1,b_1\in\mathbb Q$ with $a_1,b_1<0$ such that $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v$ is a division algebra exactly at the height-one primes $v$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ containing $\bar r$. Let $R_1$ be an Eichler order of level $N$, i.e. an intersection $\Lambda_1\cap\Lambda_2$ of two maximal orders with relative index $N$ in $\Lambda_1$; let $\iota_0:\mathbb H\to M_2(K_0)$ be an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra map; let $v$ be a height-one prime containing $r$. Let $\Gamma_t$ be the subgroup whose elements are those of [`CerednikDrinfeld.CosetGraph.awayUnits R₁ v`](def/CerednikDrinfeld_CosetGraphAtPrime.html#L37), the intersection over all $w\neq v$ of the preimages under `toLoc w` of the subgroup generated by the local box units of $R_1$ at $w$; let $\rho_0:\mathbb H^\times\to \mathrm{PGL}_2(K_0)$ be the projectivisation of $\iota_0$ on units, and $\Gamma_t'$ the subgroup of those $x\in\Gamma_t$ with $vdet$ of $\iota_0(x)$ even. Then for every vertex $w$ of the lattice tree of $(\mathcal O,K_0)$ (a homothety class of full lattices) the set of $g\in\rho_0(\Gamma_t')$ with $g\cdot w=w$ is finite, and there is a finite set $S$ of vertices such that every vertex $w$ admits $g\in\rho_0(\Gamma_t')$ with $g\cdot w\in S$.
--
--   This is the discreteness (finite vertex stabilisers) and cocompactness (finitely many vertex orbits) of the even part of the away-from-$v$ unit group of an Eichler order acting on the Bruhat–Tits tree of $\mathrm{PGL}_2(K_0)$, the group-theoretic input on the quaternionic side of the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation. It is used in the construction of the $r$-adic quotient of the formal upper half plane and in the identification of the resulting moduli problem.
